# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# ── Files that SHELL reads must be LF, always (#205) ────────────────────────
# `* text=auto` above stores LF in the repo but checks out native line endings,
# and this is a Windows box with core.autocrlf=true. So these arrive as CRLF,
# and a carriage return is invisible until it changes behaviour.
#
# It already did. #201 added `.claude/hooks/dw-project` holding the Citadel
# project name. The canonical pre-commit hook reads it with `read -r PROJECT`,
# which does NOT strip the trailing \r, so the project name became
# "Field_Compass\r" and the API query became a malformed URL:
#
#     curl ".../projects/Field_Compass\r/tasks"   ->  HTTP 000
#     curl ".../projects/Field_Compass/tasks"     ->  HTTP 200
#
# pre-commit reads the empty response as a service outage and refuses every
# commit with "Citadel unreachable" while Citadel is answering health checks
# in 0.22s. The fix shipped broken and its verification passed, because the
# file was tested as WRITTEN (LF) rather than as CHECKED OUT (CRLF).
#
# Shell scripts are the same hazard: bash on a CRLF script fails with the
# famously unhelpful `$'\r': command not found`. Both tracked .sh files here
# were CRLF.
#
# Nothing on this project needs CRLF, so pin LF wherever a shell will read it.
.claude/hooks/dw-project text eol=lf
*.sh                     text eol=lf
